Ollie presses his hands against the cut. It isn't enough.
Dodong: It's wet... Ollie, why won't it stop?
Ollie: Don't look at it. Look at me.
Dodong: I'm cold.
Ollie: I know. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
He tears a strip from his sleeve and ties it. The cloth darkens almost at once.
Ollie: I should have brought something. Anything.
Ollie: It's my fault.
=> END